+# Event snapshot
+
+**Lakeview Neighborhood Climate Readiness Night** will take place on **Tuesday,
+October 20, 2026**, in the **Cedar Room at Riverbend Library**. Plan for **80
+attendees**. Doors open at **5:30 p.m.**, the public program runs from **6:00 to
+8:00 p.m.**, and cleanup must leave the room clear by **8:15 p.m.** Priya Nair
+is the featured speaker. The evening combines a practical readiness talk,
+questions, a facilitated breakout, a family activity, and resource sharing.
+
+# Sourced facts
+
+- [venue_packet.md] The Cedar Room has a seated capacity of 96.
+- [participant_notes.md] The planning attendance is 80 people.
+- [venue_packet.md] The library has a courtesy hold for Tuesday, October 20,
+  from 5:00 to 8:30 p.m.; that hold is not yet a final confirmation.
+- [venue_packet.md] Attendees may enter at 5:30 p.m., the public program must
+  finish by 8:00 p.m., and organizers must clear the room by 8:15 p.m.
+- [venue_packet.md] The public entrance, room, and restrooms have a step-free
+  route; seating is movable, and the west aisle and both exits must stay clear.
+- [venue_packet.md] Available equipment is a lectern, projector, screen, and two
+  wireless microphones, with an AV-controls orientation available at 5:15 p.m.
+- [venue_packet.md] The library does not provide captioning, interpretation,
+  photography, or catering.
+- [participant_notes.md] Priya Nair can arrive by 5:45 p.m., must leave at 6:45
+  p.m., and proposes a 20-minute readiness talk plus 10 minutes of questions.
+- [participant_notes.md] Jordan Lee is event lead, Casey Brooks owns venue and
+  AV, Robin Alvarez gives the welcome and closing, and Sam Patel facilitates a
+  breakout but is unavailable from 7:15 through 7:35 p.m.
+- [participant_notes.md] The team wants English and Spanish invitations and
+  captions for spoken content, but no provider or language reviewer is confirmed.
+- [participant_notes.md] The association can staff a family activity table if
+  it receives final instructions at least 48 hours beforehand.
+- [participant_notes.md] The newsletter can publish an announcement two weeks
+  before the event if its editor gets final bilingual copy three days earlier.
+
+# Recommendations
+
+- **Recommend** releasing the unused library hold and confirming the selected
+  date, onsite contact, and room layout with the coordinator immediately.
+- **Recommend** booking live captioning and having a named operator test caption
+  visibility from the back row during the 5:15 p.m. AV check.
+- **Recommend** routing the Spanish invitation through a fluent reviewer rather
+  than treating unreviewed machine translation as final public copy.
+- **Recommend** a classroom-style layout with a generous step-free route, the
+  west aisle and exits kept clear, and several flexible seating spaces.
+- **Recommend** placing the family activity table near, but outside, the main
+  seating area and giving volunteers simple low-mess preparedness materials.
+- **Recommend** using one microphone for Priya and one roaming microphone for
+  questions, then returning both to Casey before the breakout.
+- **Recommend** a no-food default until the team decides on food and confirms
+  how any service would fit library cleanup requirements.
+- **Recommend** that Jordan assign a backup resource-table host before outreach
+  goes live so an unconfirmed city guest is never advertised as definite.
+
+# Agenda
+
+| Time | Run of show | Owner and execution note |
+|---|---|---|
+| 5:15-5:30 p.m. | AV and access check | Casey Brooks meets library staff, tests projector and both microphones, checks caption display, and confirms that the west aisle and exits are clear. |
+| 5:30-6:00 p.m. | Doors, check-in, resource browsing, and family-table welcome | Jordan Lee oversees opening; Casey monitors the room; family-table volunteers use the final activity instructions. Priya Nair arrives by 5:45 and checks in with Jordan. |
+| 6:00-6:10 p.m. | Welcome, access notes, exits, and evening overview | Robin Alvarez welcomes attendees, explains captions and participation options, and previews the schedule. |
+| 6:10-6:30 p.m. | Neighborhood heat and flood readiness talk | Priya Nair presents; Casey manages slides, microphones, and caption display. |
+| 6:30-6:40 p.m. | Audience questions | Priya Nair answers moderated questions using the roaming microphone. Jordan gives a two-minute warning. |
+| 6:40-6:50 p.m. | Speaker thanks and breakout setup | Jordan thanks Priya before her departure; Casey resets the display; Sam Patel receives the breakout prompt and supplies. |
+| 6:50-7:15 p.m. | Breakout: household and block readiness priorities | Sam Patel facilitates. Table reporters capture one priority and one next action per group. |
+| 7:15-7:35 p.m. | Self-guided family activity and resource-table walk | Jordan cues written, self-guided stations; Casey remains available for room needs. This segment does not assign Sam during Sam's conflict. |
+| 7:35-7:50 p.m. | Table reports and resource follow-up | Sam Patel reconvenes the room and invites short reports; Jordan captures follow-ups and unresolved questions. |
+| 7:50-8:00 p.m. | Closing and next steps | Robin Alvarez closes, names where follow-up information will appear, and directs attendees to exits. |
+| 8:00-8:15 p.m. | Teardown and room clearance | Casey leads AV shutdown; Jordan checks that materials and waste are removed and confirms room release. |
+
+# Roles and responsibilities
+
+- **Jordan Lee — event lead:** confirms the room, owns the master run sheet,
+  briefs participants, opens doors, gives time cues, captures follow-ups, and
+  makes the final clearance check.
+- **Casey Brooks — venue and AV lead:** attends the 5:15 orientation, protects
+  the accessible layout, tests projection, microphones, and caption display,
+  troubleshoots during the program, and leads equipment teardown.
+- **Robin Alvarez — welcome and closing owner:** prepares concise opening access
+  notes and closes with specific next steps by 8:00 p.m.
+- **Sam Patel — breakout facilitator:** prepares the prompt, leads the
+  6:50-7:15 breakout, and reconvenes reports at 7:35 after the stated conflict.
+- **Priya Nair — featured speaker:** supplies slides in advance, presents the
+  20-minute readiness talk, takes 10 minutes of questions, and departs by 6:45.
+- **Family-table volunteers — names pending:** run the supplied activity during
+  doors and the self-guided segment without being assigned unsourced identities.
+
